# Database migrations

StockBridge uses Flask-Migrate/Alembic. Production startup runs `flask db upgrade` and never calls `db.create_all()`.

## Existing local database

Older StockBridge builds created tables directly. Back it up, then mark the matching initial schema as applied:

```bash
python scripts/backup.py
flask db stamp 0001_initial
flask db upgrade
```

Do not run the initial upgrade against an existing populated database before stamping it, because its tables already exist.

## Brand-new database

```bash
flask db upgrade
```

## Future model changes

```bash
flask db migrate -m "Describe the schema change"
flask db upgrade
```

Inspect every generated migration, test upgrade and downgrade on a disposable database, then commit it.
